==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|NL.}} *palliativus < {{ML.}} {{term|palliare||to cloak}} < {{etyl|la}} {{term|pallium|lang=la||a cloak}}.

===Pronunciation===
*{{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpalɪətɪv/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Minimising the progression of a [[disease]] and relieving [[undesirable]] [[symptoms]] for as long as possible, rather than attempting to cure the (usually [[incurable]]) disease.

====Related terms====
* [[palliate]]
* [[palliation]]

====Translations====
{{trans-top|reducing progression and relieving symptoms}}
* Czech: {{t-|cs|paliativní}}
{{trans-mid}}
* Greek: {{t+|el|καταπραϋντικό|n|tr=katapra'intikó}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Something that [[palliate]]s, particularly a palliative [[medicine]]
#: ''The radiation and chemotherapy were only '''palliatives'''.''

